DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261003T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261003T141500
SUMMARY:Scenic AVL - Hendersonville - with WNC American Pilgrims on the Ca
 mino
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**Overview:** This hike is offered
  as a monthly training hike with the WNC Asheville Chapter of the associat
 ion of American Pilgrims on the Camino. The route has been announced on th
 e WNC Camino Group [Facebook Group Page](https://www.facebook.com/groups/A
 VLCamino/announcements).\nIf you are unfamiliar with the Camino\, here are
  a few links to learn more:\n\n*[American Pilgrims on the Camino](https://
 americanpilgrims.org/iwpmap_directory/western-north-carolina/)\n- [Stingy 
 Nomads Camino](https://stingynomads.com/camino-de-santiago-walking-guide/)
 \n*[Gronze Camino Planner](https://www.gronze.com/)\n\n**Distance:** 5\, 7
 \, or 11 miles\n**Pace: 3.2 mph**\n\n**Start Times**\n**9:00 am**- Meet at
  First Congregational Church\, 1735 5th Ave W\, Hendersonville\, NC\n**10:
 45 - 11:00 - Southern Streams coffee across from the FCC church.**\n\nFirs
 t Section: The first section is a five mile loop. The loop ends at Souther
 n Streams coffee house\, which is across from the church where we start. J
 oin us here for coffee\, even if you don't have time to walk.\n\nSecond Se
 ction: Starting at about 11:15 am from Southern Streams coffee\, continue 
 through lower Laurel Park. For those who want to exit\, you can return to 
 the church on the Ecusta Trail for a total of about 7 miles.\n\nLast Secti
 on: To downtown and St. James Church\, returning via Ecusta Trail. 10.5 mi
 les total distance.\n\n**Caution:** There are a few stretches on busy road
 s where we will need to walk single file.\n\nFull Route: [Laurel Park Loop
 ](https://www.alltrails.com/explore/map/laurel-park-loop-improved-3937230?
 u=i&sh=ifwm3x)\n\nParking: We are meeting at the First Congregational Chur
 ch. Please carpool if possible.\n\nDogs: On leash the entire time. The fir
 st section is shady\, but the pavement may be hot on the last section. Ple
 ase consider your pup's feet in the heat.\n\nScenic Asheville Series: This
  hike counts as a Wildcard substitute on my Scenic Asheville Series. There
  are 9 [hikes](https://docs.google.com/document/d/11ewlUM9OV8I4npc1cNNsSYO
 nXI0QPw2isAleXdFzEbI/edit?usp=drivesdk) in the series\; hike them all and 
 receive an [attractive badge](https://docs.google.com/drawings/d/1goXUXfzU
 BqhB4_UeCxodlk4ZPeCCgqZrWK2EUJvk_vI/edit) for your backpack. Check your st
 atus [HERE](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1XUm-X1_OhxKIi8JU5rhjsW
 37cAl4yYx8yB_NEjjI5Lk/edit?gid=0#gid=0).\n\n**Questions**\nIf you have que
 stions\, call the hike leader (Gracen) at 828-290-0886.\n\n**Guests:** For
  this hike\, there are no guest restrictions. Bring them with you.\n\n**Di
 sclaimer and Release of Liability:**\nThis activity involves hiking on cit
 y streets that may have traffic and/or hiking on natural surfaces. Partici
 pants are responsible for their safety on streets and trails. The organize
 r of this trip is a volunteer and not a professional guide. The function o
 f the organizer is only to organize this trip. If you sign up or participa
 te in this event you acknowledge that you freely and voluntarily agree to 
 assume all risks of injuries\, illnesses\, and damages arising from\, as a
  result of\, and associated with this event. You are responsible for any g
 uests\, dogs or other companions you bring with you. In addition\, you ack
 nowledge that you agree to the Meetup terms: [https://www.meetup.com/terms
 ](https://www.meetup.com/terms)
